# Effect 3 → 4 migration plan for `apps/ai-hero`

Source: the AI Hero launch desk's Effect 4 migration brief (2026-10-29).
Researched 2026-10-29 at main `902897a3`, against the Effect source at tag `effect@4.0.6` (packages/effect `4.0.6`, the stack's exact Effect pin).

## Verdict

- **Slices work. No big bang is needed.** The 89 Effect files form 12 closed import groups. TypeScript refuses any v3/v4 mix at a group boundary, so each slice proves its own edges.
- **Transition vehicle: keep `effect` on v3 and add a temporary `effect4: npm:effect@4.0.6` alias.** Migrated files import `effect4`. The last slice flips `effect` to `4.0.6`, renames `effect4` → `effect` and drops the alias. (This is the reverse of the `effect3` alias the brief offered. The reasons are below.)
- **The API surface is small.** Nine modules: `Effect`, `Either`, `Data`, `Layer`, `Context`, `Console`, `Fiber`, `Exit`, `Deferred`. No `Schema`, `Runtime`, `Option`, `Stream` or `@effect/*` anywhere. About 600 call sites need a rename. One runtime behaviour changes and needs review (the `runPromise`/`runSync` rejection value), listed under "Behaviour deltas".
- **Slice 1 (operator scripts, 12 files) is done** on `worker/effect4` (commit `e9337471`): typecheck green, held-exit tests 127/127, full suite at parity with main.

## Inventory (corrects the brief)

The brief counted 67 files. A grep for `from 'effect'` under `apps/ai-hero/{src,scripts}` finds **89** (the difference is mostly tests). The import graph (direct edges between Effect files) gives these closed groups:

| # | Group | Files | Rename-sensitive tokens* | Money? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| A | Evergreen offer journey: `evergreen-offer-journey/**`, `drovr-evergreen-{claim,coupon}*`, `evergreen-offer-status.fixtures`, `test-principals/test-principal-coupon`, `server/evergreen-pilot*`, `inngest/functions/evergreen-bridge-runtime` | 57 | 447 | **yes**: coupon executor, claim, coupon authority |
| B | Email course: `email-course/**`, `email-course-drizzle-ledger*`, `email-course-drovr-parity-receipt-sink*` | 10 | 25 | no |
| C | Held-exit scripts: `scripts/held-exit-{kit-scan,recover}.ts` + 5 tests in `src/scripts/` | 7 | 13 | no |
| D | Front desk + team invoice: `app/api/front-desk/{hooks,pricing-facts,pricing-facts-source,pricing-facts.test}.ts`, `lib/team-invoice/team-invoice-server.ts` | 5 | 30 | **yes**: `team-invoice-server.buyer()` runs a v3 program on `PricingFactsSource` and feeds `existingSeats` into team invoice pricing |
| E | Contact integrity: lib, mysql test, `src/scripts/contact-integrity-maintenance.ts` | 3 | 0 | no |
| F–G | `inngest/functions/newsletter-{provider-pause,sender-config}.ts` (Kit shadow-newsletter send path) | 1 + 1 | 8 | no, but a live Kit path |
